      },
      "worked": "Both logarithms require $x\\ne0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\ln(x^2)+\\ln(x^4)&=\\ln(x^6)\\\\\\ln(x^6)&=12\\\\x^6&=e^{12}\\\\x&=\\pm e^2\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth values are nonzero and give $\\ln(x^2)+\\ln(x^4)=4+8=12$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
